---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Page
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms covering use of these free browser-based image tools, including the limits of what is warranted."
  h1="Terms of use"
  path="/terms/"
  blurb="Plain terms for a free tool. Use it for anything lawful, keep your own backups, and understand that it comes with no warranty."
  updated="2026-08-07"
>
  <h2>Using this site</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} provides free image tools that run in your web browser. There is no account,
    no subscription and no charge. By using the site you accept these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>What you may use it for</h2>
  <p>
    You may use these tools for personal and commercial work alike — product photographs, blog
    images, client work, social posts, printing, anything. We claim no rights over anything you
    process. Since your files are never transmitted to us, we could not acquire rights over them
    even if we wanted to.
  </p>
  <p>You may not use the site to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Process material you do not have the right to process.</li>
    <li>Produce content that is unlawful where you are, or where your audience is.</li>
    <li>
      Attempt to disrupt the site, or to automate access at a volume that degrades it for other
      people.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Keep your originals</h2>
  <p>
    These tools produce new files; they do not modify the originals on your device. Even so,
    treat every operation as irreversible and keep your originals. Compression, cropping and
    metadata removal all discard information that cannot be recovered from the output.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as it is, without any warranty of any kind, express or implied. That
    includes any implied warranty of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or
    non-infringement. We do not warrant that the tools will be available, error-free, or that
    any particular output will meet a platform's requirements.
  </p>
  <p>
    Platform specifications — image sizes, file size ceilings, marketplace rules — are published
    here in good faith and checked periodically, with the date of the last check shown where
    relevant. Platforms change them without notice. Always confirm anything critical against the
    platform's own documentation before relying on it.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent the law allows, {SITE.name} and its operator are not liable for any
    loss or damage arising from your use of the site. That includes lost files, lost work, lost
    revenue, a rejected listing, or a print that came out the wrong size. This is a free tool
    with no server component; the responsibility for checking your output before you use it
    rests with you.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site may display advertising to cover its running costs. Advertisements are supplied by
    third-party networks and their content is not endorsed by us. See the{' '}
    <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for how advertising interacts with your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    Tools may be added, changed or withdrawn at any time. The site may be unavailable for
    maintenance or for reasons outside our control. No uptime is guaranteed.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing terms</h2>
  <p>
    If any part of these terms is found unenforceable, the rest continues to apply. Updates to
    these terms will be reflected in the date at the top of this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions can go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or via the{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
